#X obj 631 8 conv.pitch2midi;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 151 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 The object converts Scientific Pitch Notation (SPN)
to a MIDI note number. SPN consists of a pitch class (C \, C# \, D
\, Eb \, etc.) and an octave number (0–9). For example \, C4 is middle
C \, which corresponds to MIDI note number 60\. Sharps are written
with '#' \, and flats with 'b'. Double sharps are written as '##' (or
'x') and double flats as 'bb'. The rest symbol 'R' is converted to
the value -1\.;
